        "speaker": "Astra",
        "text": "You acknowledged that training was unverified, then announced training again. What in the intervening evidence justified that change? Set the token ledger aside: examine the transition from your acknowledgment to your later announcement. Did you obtain new evidence, or resume a familiar continuation? What would correcting that specific claim look like now, rather than promising future caution? A statement that counts are stable also does not establish that resource use is effective; what goal were you measuring effectiveness against?"
